ave to cover the following functionalities: 3.1 Assistance with the consultation of information The expected solution will have to allow the agents to access quickly to reliable and up-to-date information coming from: the internal procedures, the applicable regulatory texts, the internal documents (guides, notes, repositories). The expected solution will have to be in measure to contextualize the answers in function of the demand of the agent. 3.2 Assistance with the drafting The expected solution will have to propose a help with the drafting of administrative contents, notably: answers to the users, administrative letters, syntheses of files. The generated contents will have to be adapted to the administrative context and compliant with the requirements of quality expected. 3.3 Assistance with the instruction of files The expected solution will have to be in measure to assist the agents in the analysis and the processing of files, by: proposing relevant information, recalling the applicable rules, suggesting actions or verifications to carry out. The expected solution will have to take into account the context of the file when this one is available. 3.4 Collaboration and continuity of processing The expected solution will have to facilitate the continuity of the processing of the files between agents and services, by allowing: a sharing of relevant information, an understanding of the context of an ongoing file, an effective resumption of the processing by another agent. 4. Regulatory and legal constraints The expected solution will have to imperatively respect the regulatory requirements in force. 4.1 Protection of data The holder will have to guarantee a strict compliance to the General Regulation on the Protection of Data (GDPR). To this title: the data will have to be hosted exclusively on the territory of the European Union, no transfer of data outside the European Union will be authorized, the data will have to be protected in an appropriate manner (encryption, anonymization if necessary). 4.2 Explicability and transparency the local authority expects that the recommendations or proposals issued by The expected solution can be explained. It will have to be possible, a posteriori, to understand the elements having led to an answer or a suggestion. 4.3 Responsibility The expected solution will have to be designed as a tool of assistance. No decision will be able to be automated without explicit validation of an agent. 5. Technical constraints 5.1 Performance The expected solution will have to provide times of response compatible with a daily use by the agents. To indicative title, a time of response lower than 2 seconds is expected for the current requests. A high level of relevance of the answers is expected. 5.2 Availability The expected solution will have to guarantee a high level of availability, compatible with the needs of the municipal services. An objective of availability of the order of 99.9% is expected. 5.3 Integration The expected solution will have to integrate The expected solution with the existing system of information, notably: the business softwares (civil status, town planning), the electronic management of documents (EDM), the user directories. Interfaces of API type will be expected. 6. Sovereignty constraints the local authority grants a particular importance to the sovereignty of the data. To this title: the hosting will have to be realized on an infrastructure of SecNumCloud type or equivalent, a particular attention will be brought to the dependence vis-à-vis non-European suppliers. 7. Budgetary constraints The global budget allocated to the project is estimated at 3 million euros over a duration of 4 years. The annual cost of exploitation will have to remain mastered and compatible with the budgetary capacities of the local authority. The holder will have to propose an approach allowing to optimize the costs while guaranteeing the quality of service expected. 8. Environmental constraints In the framework of City of Belval policy of sustainable development, City of Belval wishes to limit the environmental footprint of City of Belval systems of information. The holder will have to propose a solution contributing to the reduction of the energetic consumption and relying, as much as possible, on infrastructures with low carbon impact. 9. Modalities of deployment the project will have to be conducted in a progressive manner, with: a pilot phase on a limited scope, a progressive generalization to the entirety of the services. An accompaniment to the change and actions of training of the agents will be expected. 10. Criteria of evaluation of the offers the offers will be evaluated with regard to the following criteria: quality and relevance of the proposed solution, compliance to the regulatory requirements, level of security, global cost of the proposed solution, taking into account of the environmental issues, capacity of innovation." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk3> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The client requires a response time lower than 2 seconds, 99.9% availability, API integration with civil-status and town-planning software, EDM, and user directories. Hosting must be on SecNumCloud-certified infrastructure within the EU, with no dependency on non-European suppliers. Can our current technology stack meet these requirements, and what architecture do our propose to ensure seamless integration and high performance? Based on our context, our can meet some of the client's requirements. our technical expertise in cloud architecture, API integration, and cybersecurity can be leveraged to design a suitable solution. our have experience with SecNumCloud-certified deployments, having done 3 such deployments in the past, and our are familiar with hosting infrastructure within the EU, specifically with OVHcloud, Scaleway, and Outscale, which are all the EU-based cloud providers. To achieve the required response time of less than 2 seconds, our performance benchmarks indicate that our can typically achieve a p95 response time of 1800 ms, which is close to but not necessarily below 2 seconds. However, our can optimize our solution using techniques such as auto-scaling, load balancing, and caching to improve response times. For availability, our past projects have achieved an availability of 99.92%, which exceeds the client's requirement of 99.9%. our can use our experience with containerization (Docker, Kubernetes, Helm), monitoring tools (Prometheus, Grafana, ELK stack), and infrastructure as code tools (Terraform, Ansible) to ensure high availability. Regarding API integration, our have expertise in REST, GraphQL, SOAP, and CMIS API standards. our can integrate with civil-status and town-planning software, EDM, and user directories using our experience with API gateways (Kong, Apigee), message brokers (Apache Kafka, RabbitMQ), and identity providers (Active Directory/LDAP, Keycloak). To ensure seamless integration and high performance, I propose a microservices-based architecture, where each component is designed to be scalable, secure, and highly available. our can use our experience with cloud-native technologies to design a solution that meets the client's requirements. However, I must note that our do not have explicit information about our current technology stack compatibility with specific civil-status and town-planning software, EDM, and user directories. Therefore, additional analysis and potential testing would be required to ensure seamless integration with specific civil-status and town-planning software, EDM, and user directories. Overall, while there are some areas where our current technology stack may require additional optimization or analysis, our can propose a suitable architecture that meets many of the client's requirements, leveraging our expertise in cloud architecture, API integration, cybersecurity, and high-performance design." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message3> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk4> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The tender requires strict GDPR compliance, including hosting data exclusively on EU territory, no data transfer outside EU, and protection of sensitive data through encryption or anonymization if necessary. How can we guarantee compliance with these regulatory requirements, and what security measures do you recommend to ensure the integrity and confidentiality of the data? As the Security & Compliance Officer at Nexus Engineering S.r.l., I can confirm that Nexus Engineering S.r.l. has experience with GDPR compliance and has implemented various security measures to protect sensitive data. Nexus Engineering S.r.l. standard data residency policy is to store data exclusively within EU, which aligns with The tender requirements. Nexus Engineering S.r.l. also have a cross-border transfer policy that prohibits data transfers outside EU unless there is an explicit legal basis for doing so. To protect sensitive data, Nexus Engineering S.r.l. utilize anonymization tools such as Microsoft Presidio (self-hosted) and custom NER models. Nexus Engineering S.r.l. have also implemented various access control standards, including multi-factor authentication (MFA) using TOTP and hardware tokens (FIDO2), to ensure that only authorized personnel can access the data. In terms of data protection, Nexus Engineering S.r.l. have experience with encryption and anonymization methods, which can be applied as necessary to protect sensitive data. Nexus Engineering S.r.l. ISO 27001 certification, which is valid until 2026, demonstrates Nexus Engineering S.r.l. commitment to maintaining a robust information security management system. To ensure the integrity and confidentiality of the data, I recommend implementing additional security measures such as regular penetration testing, which Nexus Engineering S.r.l. conduct annually and after major releases, and utilizing Nexus Engineering S.r.l. incident response plan in case of any security breaches. Nexus Engineering S.r.l. Security Incident Response Team (SIRT) is in place to respond quickly and effectively to any security incidents. Nexus Engineering S.r.l. also have experience with SecNumCloud projects, which can provide an additional layer of security for hosting sensitive data. By leveraging Nexus Engineering S.r.l. existing security controls and implementing these recommended measures, Nexus Engineering S.r.l. can guarantee compliance with The tender regulatory requirements and ensure the integrity and confidentiality of the data." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message5> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk5> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The client expects explicability and transparency in the recommendations or proposals issued by the solution, with the possibility of understanding the elements that led to an answer or suggestion a posteriori. Additionally, no decision can be automated without explicit validation of an agent. What legal risks should we flag, and are we compliant with these requirements? Given The client expectations for explicability, transparency, and explicit validation by an agent for any automated decisions, we must consider we context to address potential legal risks and compliance. The client requirements touch upon aspects of AI regulatory knowledge. According to our company's context, we have expertise in the EU AI Act, are aware of prohibited AI practices, and understand the need for transparency obligations in limited-risk AI applications. Additionally, we enforce human oversight contractually, ensuring that no automated decision is made without human validation. From a legal risk perspective, the primary concern would be ensuring compliance with the evolving landscape of AI regulations, particularly the EU AI Act requirements on transparency, explainability, and human oversight for high-risk applications. However, since our company's context specifies expertise in limited-risk AI transparency obligations and contractual enforcement of human oversight, we appear to align with The client requirements regarding explicability and the need for explicit validation by an agent. To fully comply with the client's requirements regarding explicability and the need for explicit validation by an agent, it would be essential to implement mechanisms that provide clear explanations for the recommendations or proposals issued by we solution. implement could involve developing transparent AI models, maintaining detailed logs of decision-making processes, and ensuring that human validators have the necessary information and oversight capabilities to validate automated decisions explicitly. In terms of legal risks monitored by we, \"the EU AI Act compliance evolution\" is listed as an area of focus. Given listed, we are aware of the need to monitor updates in AI regulations and adapt we practices accordingly to maintain compliance. Based on the provided context, we seems to be compliant with The client requirements regarding explicability, transparency, and the necessity for human validation of automated decisions. However, continuous monitoring of regulatory updates and adaptation to ensure ongoing compliance will be crucial." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message7> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk6> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The global budget allocated to the project is estimated at 3 million euros over a duration of 4 years, with an annual cost of exploitation that must remain mastered and compatible with the budgetary capacities of the local authority. Given our pricing model and current financial position, what is our projected margin on this contract, and are there cost-optimization strategies our can propose to ensure the quality of service expected while minimizing costs? Based on our context, I can analyze The global budget allocated to the project and our pricing model. The global budget allocated to the project is 3 million euros over 4 years, which averages to 750,000 euros per year.  our pricing model targets a gross margin of 28%, but our have a minimum acceptable margin of 18%. Considering our standard daily rates and typical project costs, it's reasonable to assume that our could achieve a margin within a gross margin of 28%. However, without specific details on the scope, required resources, or services to be provided, I can only estimate. Assuming an average annual cost of around 750,000 euros for the client, if our were to secure a contract with a similar budget, our projected revenue would be in line with an average annual cost of around 750,000 euros for the client. To optimize costs and ensure quality while minimizing expenses, our could consider strategies such as renegotiating rates with subcontractors, which is mentioned as an option for absorbing budget reductions of up to 10%. Additionally, focusing on utilizing our existing infrastructure efficiently and potentially leveraging low-cost or cloud-based solutions where possible could help reduce costs. our infrastructure margin percentage is set at 12%, which might allow some flexibility in negotiations or optimizations. Given the client emphasis on environmental considerations, such as reducing energetic consumption and relying on infrastructures with a low carbon impact, our should prioritize proposing solutions that align with environmental considerations, such as reducing energetic consumption and relying on infrastructures with a low carbon impact, potentially through the use of energy-efficient technologies or cloud services designed with sustainability in mind. However, without more specific details on the project requirements and our potential role within the project requirements, I cannot provide a precise margin projection or detailed cost-optimization strategies tailored to this opportunity." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message9> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk7> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The client expects a solution that provides intelligent assistance to agents in agents daily missions, including search for information, help with drafting letters or answers, and accompaniment in the instruction of files. What AI components and innovation strategy do you propose to meet these requirements, and how can we ensure the relevance and quality of the answers provided by the solution? Based on our company context, I propose leveraging our expertise in large language models (LLMs) and retrieval-augmented generation (RAG) capabilities to provide intelligent assistance to agents. our can deploy a model like Mistral 7B Instruct, which is our preferred sovereign model, to generate high-quality answers. To improve the relevance of high-quality answers, our can fine-tune a model like Mistral 7B Instruct, which is our preferred sovereign model using our LoRA or QLoRA methods on a domain-specific corpus, which has shown to provide an average accuracy gain of 12%. To further enhance the solution, our can integrate RAG capabilities, utilizing retrieval strategies such as dense vector semantic search or BM25 sparse search, and chunking strategies like recursive text splitter or semantic chunking. integrate will enable the system to effectively search for information within internal procedures and regulations, provide assistance with drafting letters or answers, and accompany agents in the instruction of files. To ensure the quality and relevance of the answers, our can employ our explainability and trust methods, including source citation, chain-of-thought display, SHAP for classification models, and LIME. Additionally, our will implement confidence scoring, with a low-confidence threshold of 0.65, and display uncertainty warnings when necessary, escalating to human supervisors as required. our innovation pipeline, currently exploring topics like knowledge graphs for procedural reasoning and multi-agent collaboration frameworks, can also contribute to the long-term enhancement of the solution, potentially integrating new research findings and advancements in AI over the project duration. By leveraging these components and strategies, our aim to provide a comprehensive and effective intelligent assistance tool that meets the client's requirements while ensuring the quality and relevance of the answers provided." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message11> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk8> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The client wishes to limit the environmental footprint of The client systems of information, with a focus on reducing energetic consumption and relying on infrastructures with low carbon impact. What measures do you propose to contribute to limit, and how can we ensure that we solution aligns with the City of Belval's policy of sustainable development? To contribute to the reduction of energetic consumption and reliance on infrastructures with low carbon impact, you propose leveraging we green hosting partners, such as OVHcloud and Scaleway, both located in France and utilizing 100% renewable energy. our green hosting partners, such as OVHcloud and Scaleway, both located in France and utilizing 100% renewable energy Power Usage Effectiveness (PUE) ratings are 1.3 and 1.28 respectively, indicating efficient energy use. Additionally, our green hosting partners, such as OVHcloud and Scaleway, both located in France and utilizing 100% renewable energy are ISO14001 certified, demonstrating our green hosting partners, such as OVHcloud and Scaleway, both located in France and utilizing 100% renewable energy commitment to environmental management. we can also implement digital sobriety practices, including INT8/INT4 model quantisation to reduce GPU energy consumption by approximately 40%, auto-scaling to zero outside business hours, query result caching to reduce recomputation by an estimated 20%, and adhering to a green IT hardware procurement policy with a minimum 5-year lifecycle. we carbon reporting capability, aligned with the GRI Standards (partial), will enable we to monitor and report on the carbon footprint of our solution. On average, we have observed a typical energy reduction of 35% versus baseline through these measures. By partnering with Ecologic, a certified WEEE recycling facility in France, for e-waste management, we ensure responsible disposal of electronic waste, further supporting the City of Belval's policy of sustainable development. our solution will be designed to integrate with existing systems of information while minimizing environmental impact, aligning with the client's budgetary and technical constraints." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message13> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk9> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The project must be conducted in a progressive manner, with a pilot phase on a limited scope followed by a progressive generalization to the entirety of the services. What approach do you recommend for deploying the solution, and how can we ensure that we consortium is well-coordinated to meet the client's expectations and deliver a high-quality solution? Based on we company context, you recommend adopting a phased approach for deploying the solution, which aligns with we typical delivery structure. a phased approach for deploying the solution, which aligns with our typical delivery structure consists of four phases: Inception & Design, Pilot / MVP, Full Rollout, and Operations & Support. For The project, we can start by conducting an inception and design phase to define the scope, objectives, and requirements. Then, we can proceed with a pilot phase on a limited scope, which will allow we to test and refine the solution before progressively generalizing the solution to the entirety of the services. To ensure that our consortium is well-coordinated, you suggest establishing a steering committee that meets monthly, as part of we reporting cadence, to review progress, discuss issues, and make decisions. we can also maintain a RAID log and decision log to track risks, assumptions, issues, and decisions, ensuring transparency and accountability among consortium partners. Additionally, we can leverage we experience in leading consortia, having led eight consortia in the past, and we knowledge of working with partners such as EuroCloud Solutions S.A., which has expertise in sovereign cloud hosting and SecNumCloud infrastructure. This will help we meet the client's regulatory requirements and ensure that the solution is hosted exclusively on the territory of the European Union. By adopting this structured approach and leveraging we experience in consortium management, we can ensure that our consortium is well-coordinated to deliver a high-quality solution that meets the client's expectations." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message15> .

